{
  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC MEASUREMENT VECTORS. There is not a single photograph in this file",
    "and there must never be one.",
    "",
    "Workstream 9 asks for 40–50 permissioned real photographs with hand-verified",
    "tags. This repository has none, and the plan is explicit about what to do in",
    "that case: complete the harness, use whatever representative material exists,",
    "and record the missing sample count as a founder blocker rather than pretend",
    "catalogue images prove camera-photo quality. So the numbers below exercise",
    "every threshold and comparison in `photo-evidence-rules.ts` and",
    "`photo-match.ts`, and the suite reports 0/40 alongside them.",
    "",
    "What a synthetic vector CAN prove: that a sharpness of 59 is refused and 61",
    "accepted, that a five-bit hash difference is a duplicate and a six-bit one is",
    "not, that the fast path is unreachable without a feature print. What it",
    "CANNOT prove: that a real iPhone photograph of a real jumper in real evening",
    "light produces a sharpness the threshold treats correctly. Only the",
    "photographs can, and they do not exist yet.",
    "",
    "Real references, when they arrive, are read from a manifest OUTSIDE the",
    "repository — see the suite's docblock. No image, no signed URL and no",
    "storage path is committed here."
  ],
